  "description": "Ho-Su harbors a desire to collect “crying faces” that match his taste. Hiding this fact, he maintains a precarious friendship with his roommate, Woo-Young. Then, one day, he finds himself witnessing an unexpected scene...\n\n*“The look on Woo-Young's face while he's doing XX...”*\n\nWas it an impulse, or a long-simmering desire? By the time he came to his senses, he had already crossed a line he shouldn’t have. \n\n*“Woo-Young... Can I film you crying?”*\n\n(Source: Lezhin, translated)",
